### Runtime dependencies (not bundled; resolved from Maven Central)
WebRTC `io.github.webrtc-sdk:android` (libwebrtc, BSD-style), OkHttp (Apache-2.0), protobuf-javalite
(BSD-3-Clause), kotlinx (Apache-2.0), Dagger (Apache-2.0), jwtdecode (MIT), semver4j (MIT),
android-jain-sip-ri (public domain / NIST), AndroidX (Apache-2.0).

## Compliance note
In the compiled SDK the upstream name appears only as attribution: in this file and in the copyright
lines at the top of the derived source files (plus fork-maintenance notes under `tools/`, `doc/upstream/`
and `CHANGELOG.md`). Checked on the published artifacts: no upstream-name string in the compiled
classes, `lint.jar` or the javadoc jar; in the sources jar only the copyright lines. The deliberate exceptions are wire-protocol values that every SDK must share (see
`tools/rebrand/README.md`): `lk.*` attribute keys and the E2EE key-derivation constants.

